# Muro cloud handoffs

When the run is triggered from a Notion task (webhook, URL in prompt, or `notion_task_id` in metadata):

1. Load skill **`notion-handoff`** first, then skills listed on the linked **Agent** profile (Tasks → Agents relation; permanent key = Notion page ID). See `profiles/README.md` for name ↔ skills.
2. Re-fetch task and profile from Notion via MCP — do not rely on webhook body alone for the full spec.
3. Resolve any **work repo from the task’s Project** (never from the Agent profile). If Project has no repo, use MCP and handbook skills only — do not invent a codebase.
4. Respect **autonomy** on profile or task: `research` (read-only), `draft` (prepare changes, no publish), `pr` (open PR), `publish` (client-facing deploy only when explicitly allowed).
5. Write back to Notion: heartbeats **appended** to the active **Audit Log** run **page body** (`insert_content` at end); coarse task status on the task via properties only; blocked narrative (`Message from AI: …`) on the audit run **page body** — never `notion-create-comment` on the task; run row **Summary** property + deliverables at end; mirror final summary on task **Agent Summary** property if present (not comments).
6. For duplicate triggers: if the task already has an active run with a fresh timestamp, append idempotency notes to the audit log run page and set coarse task status only — do not comment on the task or double-execute destructive work.